\section{Turning saving off}{


\code{spades(sim, .saveInitialTime = NA)} temporarily suppresses module-level
saving without changing the \code{simList}, so the same \code{simList} can be run again
with its own values. It has no effect on the \code{outputs} table, and no effect on
a module that saves with plain \code{saveRDS()}.
}

\section{Keeping track of what was saved}{


\code{\link[=outputs]{outputs()}} on a completed simulation reports which files were written and
when. A module that saves a file its own way can add it to that table with
\code{\link[=registerOutputs]{registerOutputs()}}, so it is tracked at the \code{simList} level like any other
output -- and so \code{\link[=saveSimList]{saveSimList()}} can pick it up.
}

